pvp.innocent-surround=most likely the surround is already complete, and then there is nothing to place and that is fine
pvp.innocent-hole-filler=most likely there is no hole to fill near the target, and then that is fine
pvp.innocent-auto-web=most likely the predicted block already has a web: a web is not replaced, so against a cornered player who keeps moving away the block does not change and there is nothing more to place
pvp.innocent-default=there may be no valid position right now
pvp.suspects-crystal-aura=min-damage (6 by default: against netherite with Protection IV almost no position reaches 6 damage) and support (Disabled by default: without it, it does not place where there is not already a block below)
pvp.suspects-auto-trap=whitelist (by default it has obsidian and crying obsidian, and the netherite block is NOT on it), place-range and walls-range (4 by default, and the second one rules as soon as something is in between) and top-blocks/bottom-blocks
pvp.suspects-auto-web=place-range and walls-range (4 by default), ticks-to-predict (10 by default: a web where they will be half a second from now, not where they are) and doubles (off by default)
pvp.suspects-auto-anvil=height (2 by default: the anvil goes three blocks above their feet, and that block has to be free) and delay (10 ticks by default between one anvil and the next)
pvp.suspects-surround=blocks (by default it has obsidian, crying obsidian and netherite block, and I only count the obsidian for you) and only-on-ground
pvp.suspects-hole-filler=only-moving (on by default, and in the sources it discards the one who IS MOVING, not the one standing still), feet-range (1.5 by default from the target's feet, already predicted) and ignore-safe
pvp.suspects-default=its range and position settings
